          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The definition of
            %em cohesive topos
            or
            %em category of cohesion
            aims to axiomatize properties of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            that make it a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+topos"} gros topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
            inside of which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            may take place. See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+cohesive+toposes"} motivation for cohesive toposes
            for a non-technical discussion.
          %p
            The idea behind the term is that a
            %em geometric space
            is roughly something consisting of points or pieces that are
            %em held together
            by some cohesion - for instance by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
          %p
            The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma : \mathcal{E} \to Set
            of a cohesive topos over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            may be thought of as sending a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to its underlying set of points
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with all
            %em cohesion forgotten
            (for instance with the topology or the smooth structure forgotten)
          %p
            Conversely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Codisc
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Disc
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{Codisc}{\leftarrow}}}
                  Set
          %p
            send a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            either to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+space"} discrete space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc(S)
            with
            %em discrete
            cohesive structure (for instance with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+space"} codiscrete space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Codisc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Codisc(S)
            with the
            %em codiscrete
            cohesive structure (for instance with
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codiscrete+topology"} codiscrete topology
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+cylinder"} adjoint cylinder
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unity+of+opposites"} unity of opposites
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+being"} category of being
          %p
            Moreover, the idea is that cohesion makes points lump together to
            %em connected pieces
            \. This is modeled by one more functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0 : \mathcal{E} \to Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            this sends a cohesive space to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected components
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Pi = \pi_0)
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-topos"} (n,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            sends a cohesive space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncation
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} geometric fundamental ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            In total this gives an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Codisc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Codisc
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Disc
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Π
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi_0 \dashv Disc \dashv \Gamma \dashv Codisc) :
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\stackrel{\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\longrightarrow}}{\overset{Disc}{\leftarrow}}}{\stackrel{\underset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{Codisc}{\leftarrow}}}
                  Set
                  \\;
          %p
            A cohesive topos is a topos whose terminal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            admits an extension to such a quadruple of adjoints, satisfying some further properties.
          %p
            Notice that most objects in a cohesive topos are far from being just sets with extra structure: while the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            does produce the set of points underlying an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in the cohesive topos, it may happen that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is very non-trivial but that nevertheless
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X)
            has very few
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} points
            (possibly none, with the axioms so far). The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            that we may think of as point sets equipped with extra structure is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conc
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conc_\Gamma(\mathcal{E})
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+sheaves"} concrete sheaves
            inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi Codisc
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mi Conc
                    %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi Conc
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Set
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{Codisc}{\hookrightarrow}}
                  Conc_\Gamma(\mathcal{E})
                  \\stackrel{\overset{Conc}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\,.
          %p
            It is the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
            that allows to identify
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Conc
                      %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Conc_\Gamma(E)
          %p To ensure that there is a minimum of points, one can add further axioms. From the above adjunctions one gets a canonical natural morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma X \to \Pi_0 X
          %p
            from the points of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the set of connected pieces of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
            is demanding that
            %em each piece has at least one point
            \.
          %p
            Moreover, one can demand that the cohesive pieces of product or power spaces are the products of the cohesive pieces of the factors. For powers of a single space, this is demanding that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
            the following canonical map is an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi S
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi_0(X^S) \xrightarrow{\simeq} (\Pi_0(X))^S
                  \\,.
          %p
            For more general products, it would be a similar map
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0(\prod_i X_i) \to \prod_i \Pi_0(X_i)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+site"} cohesive site
            for concrete illustrations of these ideas.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#fundamental_axioms Fundamental axioms
          #CohesiveTopos.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              over some base topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f^* \dashv f_*) : \mathcal{E} \stackrel{\overset{f^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_*}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\mathcal{S}
            %p
              is
              %strong cohesive
              if it is a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+connected+topos"} strongly connected topos
              %li
                %p
                  and a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
            %p
              In detail this means that it has the following
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} properties
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                        %mo ⊣
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_! \dashv f^*)
                  satisfying a suitable condition;
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"} connected topos
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
                  preserves the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
              %li
                %p
                  it is
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strongly+connected+topos"} strongly connected
                  \:
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
                  preserves even all
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite"} finite
                  = succeed "s;" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %mo ⊣
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo !
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_* \dashv f^!)
                  (this is sufficient for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  to be local, since we have already assumed it to be connected);
            %p
              In summary
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is cohesive over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              if we have an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} quadruple
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo !
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↩
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↩
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo !
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_! \dashv f^* \dashv f_* \dashv f^!) :
                    \\mathcal{E}
                    \\array{
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} f_! \phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\\
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} f^\ast \phantom{AA} }{\hookleftarrow}
                    \\\
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} f_\ast \phantom{AA} }{\longrightarrow}
                    \\\
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} f^! \phantom{AA} }{\hookleftarrow}
                    }
                    \\mathcal{S}
            %p
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^!
              is, as indicated (for instance by the discussion at
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            %p
              Hence the definition of cohesion specifies two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
              and one also
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
            %p
              Since a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
              it follows with the discussion
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory#ReflectiveSubcategoriesOfCartesianClosedCategotries"} here
              that both of these are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+ideals"} exponential ideals
              = succeed "-inclusion" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
              preserves finite products.
          %p To reflect the geometric interpretation of these axioms we will here and in related entries often name these functors as follows
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Disc
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi coDisc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                              %msub
                                %mi Π
                                %mn 0
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↩
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                              %mi Disc
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                              %mi Γ
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ↩
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                              %mi coDisc
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi_0 \dashv Disc \dashv \Gamma \dashv coDisc) :
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\array{
                  \\overset{\phantom{AAA} \Pi_0 \phantom{AAA}}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\\
                  \\overset{\phantom{AA} Disc \phantom{AA} }{\hookleftarrow}
                  \\\
                  \\overset{\phantom{AAA} \Gamma \phantom{AAA} }{\longrightarrow}
                  \\\
                  \\overset{\phantom{AA} coDisc \phantom{AA} }{\hookleftarrow}
                  }
                  \\mathcal{S}
                  \\,.
          #AdjointTriple.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The above
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
              canonically induces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ʃ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo ♭
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Γ
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mi Disc
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Π
                            %mn 0
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi coDisc
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
