                    {\overset{p}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathcal{C}
            %p
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              takes the unique object of the terminal category to that terminal object.
            %p
              From this it follows (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+Categories+and+Toposes#KanExtensionOfAdjointPairIsAdjointQuadruple"} this example
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              produces an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+quadruple"} adjoint quadruple
              of functors between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
